  "documentation": "Non-regression golden fixture for the v9-native call-tx composition path (packages/contracts/src/unproven-call-tx.ts -> packages/contracts/src/utils/ledger-utils.ts, createUnprovenLedgerCallTx). Captured from a real execution of the deposit circuit against the compiled shielded-map contract in src/test/resources/compiled/shielded-map/, at base commit 025133dbeec3d2aed32e335a55cde2853ee3fc12. Stage 1 (decodedContractState) is toLedgerContractState(shieldedInitialState).serialize(), hex, called directly -- real production code, no reproduction. observedAssembledCall (stages 2 and 3) is captured by calling the real, unmodified createUnprovenLedgerCallTx with our single call bound to a fixed communication commitment (fixedInputs.communicationCommitmentRand), then reading the one ContractCall it assembled back off the returned transaction's tx.intents -- the same seam the accompanying test's stage 4 uses for its structural-only checks. Nothing here reproduces createUnprovenLedgerCallTx's own argument list; every field below is read from what the function actually returned. guaranteedTranscript.effects and .program are byte-pinned (bigints/byte arrays hex-encoded for JSON). guaranteedTranscript.gas is deliberately NOT captured here: it is a cost-model number (picosecond timings, byte counters) that moves on every ledger-v9/onchain-runtime/compact-runtime bump regardless of whether composition behaviour changed, and is architecture-sensitive besides -- the accompanying test asserts only its shape (four keys, each a non-negative bigint), never its values. toStringCompactNormalized is ContractCall.toString(true) -- the Debug repr is the only aggregate, own-fields view this class exposes; it redacts communication_commitment and proof as opaque placeholders, and does not surface the key_location string ContractCallPrototype was built with (confirmed empirically absent from this repr) -- a regression there is a known, accepted blind spot of this unproven-transaction-only suite; see the accompanying test's stage 3 comment. The four gas/cost-model fields nested inside it (read_time, compute_time, bytes_written, bytes_deleted) are ALSO redacted to the fixed placeholder '<redacted-cost>' before this value is captured, for the same reason guaranteedTranscript.gas above is shape-checked rather than byte-pinned -- see the accompanying test's redactGasCostFields comment.",
